<title>UK: Bank of New York wins September Reuter forex poll.</title>
<headline>Bank of New York wins September Reuter forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of New York in London won the Reuter foreign exchange poll for September, beating 26 other contenders from across the globe in the monthly contest.</p>
<p>The average divergence of Bank of New York's exchange rate predictions from the actual rates at the end of the month was 0.83 percent.</p>
<p>FX Analytics in New York came second with a divergence of 0.99 percent followed in third, for the second month running, by DKB in London, with an average divergence of 1.06 percent.</p>
<p>Overall, the percentage difference between actual and forecasted rates varied between 0.83 and 3.69 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on September 30 of dollar/mark at 1.5268 marks, dollar/yen at 111.60 yen and sterling/dollar at $1.5646.</p>
